    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0204" n="190" sameAs="frus:frus1949v05/pg190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.4027/2–849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in France
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d104-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-08T20:00:00-05:00">February 8, 1949—8
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>375. Reurtel 401 Jan. 31.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d104-f2"/> Dept not now prepared
                    instruct Tel Aviv change instrs from info to action for fol reasons:</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item> Dept doubts efforts induce Israelis terminate Czech Airlines’ services
                        would be successful at this time since Israelis would probably be reluctant
                        take initiative and Israel not likely wish sever only scheduled internatl
                        air connection. Dept does not wish suggest Israelis terminate this service
                        when TWA or other scheduled carriers not in position resume service
                        Israel.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>In view above, believe effort should be concentrated first upon
                        termination CSA services Greece and Turkey.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item> Dept hopes for increased Amer influence Israeli civil aviation through
                        provision technical assistance various forms, thus giving US <pb facs="0205"
                            n="191" xml:id="pg191"/> more satis basis for approach Israel than now
                        exists re implementation our policy.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d104-f3"/>
                    </item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d104-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d104-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Tel Aviv, London, Bern, Athens, Ankara, and Cairo.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d104-f2" n="2" xml:id="d104-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. It inquired if, in view of the French and British <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> recognition of Israel and the possible
                    early settlement of Arab-Israeli warfare, it would be appropriate actively to
                    seek Israeli adherence to U.S.-U.K. civil aviation policy toward Eastern Europe
                    (711.4027/1–3149).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d104-f3" n="3" xml:id="d104-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram 966, March 14, from London, not printed, reviewed arguments for securing
                    Israeli adherence to the civil aviation policy toward Eastern Europe
                    (711.4027/3–1449). Telegram 902, March 17, to London, not printed, replied that
                    the Department of State did not feel that the time was ripe for an approach to
                    the Israeli Government, and that chances for a successful approach would be
                    greater after Western air carriers resumed scheduled service to Israel
                    (711.4027/8–1449).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
